    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d161-a1">

                <pb facs="0288" n="282" sameAs="frus:frus1901China/pg282"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    141.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. de Cologan to the Chinese
                    Plenipotentiaries.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-06-29"><hi rendition="#italic">June 29,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Highness and Your Excellency</hi>: I have the
                    honor to acknowledge receipt of your letter dated the 13th of June, in which you
                    inform us of the terms of an imperial decree suspending examinations in a
                    certain number of localities.</p>
                <p>This decree is quite in conformity with the request which the representatives of
                    the powers had instructed me to place before you.</p>
                <p>Article X of the collective note states that the decree suspending the
                    examinations shall be posted throughout the whole Empire. I request your
                    highness and your excellency, in the name of the representatives of the powers,
                    to take the necessary measures so that that formality may be complied with
                    without delay.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">B. J. de Cologan.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
